From 5af6eb1a099125681917eec6c4db0a688b0f5ee8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cindy Krafft <cynthiacondra@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 00:38:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] doc: concordance factors need unrooted species and gene trees

A rooted species tree gets NA on its root branch in --scf/--gcf and a rooted
gene tree aborts --gcf with 'Taxon not found in full tree: __root__'
(tree/discordance.cpp). Add a warning box saying so.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TaHntBDKuZJpMAAMenkC44
---
 doc/Concordance-Factor.md | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/doc/Concordance-Factor.md b/doc/Concordance-Factor.md
index 713a5a1..ec01b15 100644
--- a/doc/Concordance-Factor.md
+++ b/doc/Concordance-Factor.md
@@ -160,6 +160,9 @@ iqtree3 -te concat.treefile -s ALN_FILE --scfl 100 --prefix concord
 iqtree2 -t concat.treefile -s ALN_FILE --scf 100 --prefix concord -T 10
 ```
 	
+>**NOTE**: The species tree given with `-t`/`-te` and the gene trees given with `--gcf` must be unrooted. A Newick tree with a bifurcating root (e.g. `((A,B),(C,D));`) is read as rooted: the branch at its root then receives no concordance factor (`NA` in `.cf.stat`), and a rooted gene tree stops `--gcf` with `Taxon not found in full tree: __root__`. Unroot such trees first (e.g. write the root as a trifurcation, `(A,B,(C,D));`).
+{: .warning}
+
 `--scf` specifies the number of quartets (randomly sampled around each internal
 branch) for computing sCF. We recommend at least 100 quartets for stable sCF
 values. Note that running this command several times may lead to slightly
